defmodule <%= inspect @module %> do
  @moduledoc """
  Which UI routes a scope may navigate to.

  The single source of truth for route access, and deliberately **not**
  `Ash.can?`: a filter policy allows the action and returns no rows, so `can?`
  says yes for a page that would be empty. `<%= inspect @nav %>` names this
  module, and every rendering of the nav filters through it.

  `mix ash_quick.gen.quick_view` adds each path it routes to `@routes`. That
  list is a starting point rather than an answer: as written, every scope
  reaches every route in it. Split it by role before this application has more
  than one kind of user —

      def routes_for(%MyApp.Scope{current_user: %{role: role}}), do: routes_for_role(role)
      def routes_for(_scope), do: []

      defp routes_for_role(:admin), do: ~w(/products /users)
      defp routes_for_role(_role), do: []

  — writing each role's routes out in full. That is what makes adding a route a
  decision about which roles reach it, and leaves a role nobody opened up
  fail-closed.

  Matching is strict prefix matching: `/products` covers `/products` and
  `/products/123`, but not `/products_archive`. Two routes that mean different
  things must not share a prefix.
  """

  @behaviour AshQuick.AccessControl

  @routes []

  @impl AshQuick.AccessControl
  def routes_for(_scope), do: @routes

  @doc """
  True when `scope` may navigate to `path`.

  Either the path equals an allowed route or it sits directly under one. A
  mount-time gate calls this on every navigation.
  """
  def can_access?(scope, path) when is_binary(path) do
    scope |> routes_for() |> Enum.any?(&path_matches?(path, &1))
  end

  defp path_matches?(path, route), do: path == route or String.starts_with?(path, route <> "/")

  @doc """
  Every route any scope at all can reach, for `mix ash_quick.check`.

  Once `routes_for/1` splits by role, derive this from wherever the roles are
  declared rather than restating the paths, or it goes stale exactly when a role
  is added.
  """
  @impl AshQuick.AccessControl
  def all_routes, do: @routes
end
